    "created_at": "2024-12-09T16:42:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-12-09T16:42:58Z",
    "body": "> Yeah I guess dialog is tricky since you can already declaratively open it with the open attribute in non-modal mode, but I think that modal dialogs are used a lot more often that non-modal ones so it would make sense to have a declarative way of opening it modally.\r\n\r\nOne idea that came up in https://github.com/openui/open-ui/issues/920 was to make the open attribute an enum for dialog. So you could do `open=\"modal\"` and it would open modally.",
